 "about_text": "Junior High is a multi-purpose art gallery, event space, and artist sanctuary in Glendale, California, founded by Faye Orlove. It describes itself as a community-driven venue dedicated to arts expression and arts education for people of all ages and backgrounds. Programming spans gallery shows, music events, workshops, panels, and editorial projects, with a particular focus on supporting marginalized and emerging artists, including beginners, women, queer and nonbinary artists, and artists of color. The space, which holds over 80 people, emphasizes radical empathy, accessibility, and safety as guiding values, positioning itself as an alternative to traditional, exclusionary art-world spaces.",
